      "writtenOn": "2025-10-07T11:53:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually they are not exactly \"shadow related\". In regular KVM (w/o pKVM) these SPTE_xxx macros are used for EPT page tables as well (which are _not_ shadow page tables, they are stage-2 page tables managed solely by KVM), and generally the terms \"spte\" or \"shadow page\" refer to EPT page tables as well (so they are a bit of a misnomer), for historical reasons. https://docs.kernel.org/virt/kvm/x86/mmu.html#shadow-pages\n\nWhereas PTE_PFN_xxx macros are used by kernel for stage-1, not stage-2 page tables.\n\nSo, it\u0027s probably more consistent and reliable if in pKVM we also use SPTE_xxx (i.e. follow what KVM does for EPT), not PTE_PFN_xxx?",
